<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Avantel offers single-tariff service.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Avantel offers single-tariff service.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Avantel, one of the new telephone service operators in Mexico, launched a new service Monday offering a single long-distance tariff for residential customers, the company said.</p>
<p>Avantel, a joint venture between financial company Grupo Financiero Banamex-Accival and MCI Communications Corp, said the single-tariff service costs 1.40 pesos per minute for any call inside Mexico, 24 hours a day.</p>
<p>Avantel said the service would be added to other tariffs and discount services offered by the company.</p>
<p>((-- Chris Aspin, Mexico City Newsroom 525 7287902))</p>
